# Apple documents that the association file must be served as application/json, and it
# has NO FILE EXTENSION -- which means a static host guesses. GitHub Pages guesses
# `application/octet-stream`; verified by probing runit-legal/.nojekyll, which is why the
# site is here and not there. Cloudflare Pages lets us say it outright.
#
# This file is the entire reason the host moved. Do not drop it.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# The app itself. Its session lives in localStorage on the web route, so it must never be
# framed by another origin. No CSP here: the expo export inlines scripts and styles, and a
# policy that breaks the bundle gets deleted inside a week -- these three cost nothing.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
